Io-OTD (Icon of the Team – Outfit of the Day)
Activity Guidelines
Io-OTD is a voluntary weekly activity held every wash day (Friday) to encourage professional, creative, and confident self-expression in the workplace. Featuring monthly themes, peer voting, monthly photoshoots, and digital awards, the activity culminates in a Grand Awards Night at the end of the fiscal year to crown the Io-OTD Grand Champion.
Objectives
•	Professional Appearance: Encourage professional attire and creative self-expression within the workplace.
•	Grooming & Presentation: Promote confidence, neatness, and good personal grooming among section members.
•	Positive Culture: Foster an engaging, inclusive, and respectful work environment.
•	Recognition: Recognize employees who consistently demonstrate effort, style, and professionalism.
General Guidelines
•	Schedule: Conducted every wash day (usually Friday).
•	Participation: Voluntary and open to all section members.
•	Themes: Each month features a specific style guide with general color suggestions. The Monthly Theme will be provided every first working day of the month.
•	Company Policy Precedence: Outfits must be clean, neat, professional, and fully compliant with company policies. Company dress codes always take precedence over activity themes.
•	Spirit of Activity: Designed to be simple, fun, respectful, and lighthearted.
•	Outfit Reuse: Outfits may be repeated on different wash days, provided the styling aligns with the active theme and company dress policy.
Dress Code Restrictions (Not Allowed)
To maintain workplace professionalism, participants must avoid:
•	Revealing clothing such as crop tops, short skirts and skorts, skirts with slits, shorts, or low-cut tops.
•	See-through or transparent clothing that is inappropriate for a professional setting.
•	Dirty, torn, wrinkled, or overly casual clothing.
•	Clothing with offensive words, symbols, or images.
•	Footwear that is too casual or inappropriate, such as slippers or unprofessional sandals, unless approved by workplace policy.
•	Overly flashy or distracting accessories that may affect a neat and professional appearance.
•	Any outfit considered immodest, unsafe, or unsuitable for the work environment.
Note: If an outfit matches the theme but does not follow the company dress code, it will be disqualified.
Evaluation Criteria
Participants will be evaluated based on the following:
•	Professionalism: The outfit should reflect a polished and workplace-appropriate appearance.
•	Neatness and Grooming: Clothing should be clean, well-maintained, and properly worn. Overall grooming, including hair, makeup, and general presentation, will also be considered.
•	Appropriateness: The attire should be suitable for the workplace setting and consistent with professional standards.
•	Creativity and Style: The outfit may reflect individuality while still maintaining a professional image. Section members will consider how well clothing pieces, colors, and accessories are coordinated.
•	Confidence and Presentation: The participant should carry the outfit with confidence, composure, and professionalism.
•	Overall Appeal: Section members will assess the total appearance, including clothing, accessories, grooming, and how well the outfit fits the workplace atmosphere.
Activity Mechanics & Voting Process
1. Voting & Form Schedule
•	No Pre-Registration: Any section member physically present in their wash day outfit can be voted for. To keep voting quick and clear for our section members, the form provides pre-populated dropdown lists separated by gender (Male and Female nominees).
•	In-Person Verification: To keep the activity simple and hassle-free, no weekly photo submissions are required. The WLB Committee will casually verify the top vote recipients in person at the office before finalizing weekly results.
•	Voting Window: The voting form is open from 9:30 AM to 6:00 PM on each activity day.
•	Reminders: Automated reminders are sent out during lunch breaks to encourage participation.
•	Vote Limit: Each member may cast one submission per week, selecting two nominees: one male and one female. The form automatically restricts access to a single submission per user.
2. Committee Validation & Eligibility
•	Theme & Dress Code Verification: To ensure fairness and maintain proper standards, the WLB Committee reviews the top male and female vote recipients. Outfits that do not match the monthly theme or violate company dress codes are disqualified for that week.
•	Leaves & Remote Work: Employees on official leave, working from home (WFH), or on business travel on a wash day are excluded from that week's voting.
•	Disqualification Rule: If a participant is disqualified in a weekly poll due to dress code or theme non-compliance, all votes cast for them for that specific week are voided and will not count toward weekly titles or the fiscal year cumulative tally. If the disqualified participant was in 1st place, the weekly win automatically passes to the next highest valid vote recipient.
•	Final Authority: The committee's validation decisions regarding outfit eligibility are final.
3. Points Allocation, Tie-Breakers & Confidentiality
•	Weekly Wins & Monthly Titles: Each verified weekly win counts toward the Monthly Winner title for that calendar month.
•	Grand Champion Calculation (Cumulative Raw Votes): Every valid vote earned by a participant across all weekly voting sessions is accumulated into a running fiscal year master tally. The Grand Champion is determined by the highest overall cumulative raw vote total across the entire fiscal year.
•	Weekly Tie-Breaker: In the event of a vote tie for top male or female in a weekly poll, the WLB Committee will evaluate the tied entries against the Evaluation Criteria (Theme, Grooming, Appropriateness) to select a single Weekly Winner.
•	Monthly Tie-Breaker: If participants tie in total weekly wins within a calendar month, the Monthly Winner is awarded to the participant with the highest overall monthly vote percentage. In the rare event of an exact tie in both weekly wins and monthly vote percentage, Monthly Co-Winners will be declared for that month.
•	Fiscal Year Grand Champion Tie-Breaker: In the rare event of a tie in total cumulative raw votes at the end of the fiscal year, the tie will be broken by the highest number of Monthly Wins achieved across the year.
•	Data Confidentiality: To ensure fairness, prevent early prediction of the Grand Champion, and maintain an exciting reveal at the Grand Awards Night, exact raw vote tallies remain strictly confidential within the WLB Committee. Monthly announcements will display vote percentages only.
Selection Process and Winner Determination
1. Winner Hierarchy
•	Weekly Winner: The male and female participants with the highest valid votes each week, subject to WLB Committee validation (or Committee Evaluation in the event of a weekly tie).
•	Monthly Winner: The male and female participants who accumulate the highest number of weekly wins within the calendar month. In the event of a tie in weekly wins, the participant with the higher monthly vote percentage takes the title.
•	Fiscal Year Grand Champion: The overall male and female participants with the highest cumulative raw vote total across all weekly voting sessions throughout the entire fiscal year. Standing numbers remain strictly confidential until the ceremony.
Awards, Photoshoots & Recognition
1. End-of-Month Photoshoot
•	Participant Roster: At the end of every month, weekly winners and top nominees are invited to participate in a special photoshoot session to showcase the monthly theme.
2. Monthly Recognition
•	Digital Certificates: Official digital certificates are awarded at month-end to recognize weekly and monthly winners.
•	Monthly Announcements: Published results will highlight the Monthly Winners (1 Male, 1 Female) alongside their overall monthly vote percentage to provide full transparency while keeping overall cumulative headcounts confidential.
3. Grand Awards Night
•	Fiscal Year Celebration: Held at the end of the fiscal year to honor the overall Io-OTD Grand Champions, consistent participants, and special category titleholders (subject to organizer approval).

